00:57:08,571 --> 00:57:14,571
The Piano is a 1993 historical romance film written and
directed by New Zealand filmmaker Jane Campion.

11
01:02:51,428 --> 01:02:57,428
It stars Holly Hunter, Harvey Keitel, Sam Neill, and Anna
Paquin (in her first major acting role).

12
01:08:34,285 --> 01:08:40,285
The film focuses on a mute Scottish woman who travels to a remote part of New
Zealand with her young daughter after her arranged marriage to a settler.

13
01:14:17,142 --> 01:14:23,142
The plot has similarities to Jane Mander's 1920 novel, The Story of a
New Zealand River, but also substantial differences.

14
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
Campion has cited the novels Wuthering Heights and
The African Queen as inspirations.

15
01:25:42,857 --> 01:25:48,857
An international co-production between Australia and France, The Piano premiered at the 1993 Cannes Film Festival on May 15,
1993, where it won the Palme d'Or, rendering Campion the first female director to achieve that distinction.

16
01:31:25,714 --> 01:31:31,714
It was a commercial success, grossing US$140.2 million
worldwide against its US$7 million budget.

17
01:37:08,571 --> 01:37:14,571
The film was also noted for its crossover appeal beyond the arthouse circuit in
attracting mainstream popularity, largely due to rave reviews and word of mouth.

18
01:42:51,428 --> 01:42:57,428
The Piano earned numerous accolades, including three Academy Awards (for Hunter as Best Actress, Paquin as Best Supporting Actress, and Campion
for Best Original Screenplay), a WGA Award, a Golden Globe Award, three BAFTA Awards, and eleven Australian Film Institute Awards.

19
01:48:34,285 --> 01:48:40,285
The film explores themes of adultery, secret love,
beach, jealousy, love triangle.

20
01:54:17,142 --> 01:54:23,142
The tone is dark and emotional and intense.
